    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p5-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}=\\sqrt[12]{2}$. Hint: Evaluate $\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\right)^{12}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}=\\sqrt[12]{2}$.\n\nThe positive left side has twelfth power $2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\right)^{12}&=\\left(\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\right)^3\\right)^4\\\\\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\right)^{12}&=\\left(\\sqrt[4]{2}\\right)^4\\\\\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\right)^{12}&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}>0$, the definition of the twelfth root gives $\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt[4]{2}}=\\sqrt[12]{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 39
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Can you generalise the above result?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sqrt[m]{\\sqrt[n]{x}}=\\sqrt[mn]{x}$ for $x\\ge0$ and positive integers $m,n$.\n\nRaise the nonnegative left side to the power $mn$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ge0$ and positive integers $m,n$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\sqrt[m]{\\sqrt[n]{x}}\\right)^{mn}&=\\left(\\left(\\sqrt[m]{\\sqrt[n]{x}}\\right)^m\\right)^n\\\\\\left(\\sqrt[m]{\\sqrt[n]{x}}\\right)^{mn}&=\\left(\\sqrt[n]{x}\\right)^n\\\\\\left(\\sqrt[m]{\\sqrt[n]{x}}\\right)^{mn}&=x.\\end{align*}$$\nThe left root is nonnegative, so $\\sqrt[m]{\\sqrt[n]{x}}=\\sqrt[mn]{x}$ by the definition of an $mn$th root. The identity also holds for negative $x$ when both $m$ and $n$ are odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
